#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1121 expect=violation domain=DM
#note "FRESH. Row 1: ARMCD='Scrnfail' FIRES. The exception list is a bare quoted-literal membership test with no upper() wrapper, so it is CASE-SENSITIVE: 'Scrnfail' is not 'SCRNFAIL' and the exception does not apply. Row 2: the exact CT spelling 'SCRNFAIL' -> silent. The pair is the deciding branch of the one set operator in this rule and no twin pins it. See finding SD1121-F1 for why firing is the defensible reading. No class= on the dataset line — the twin declares none."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 USUBJID=001
dataset DM label="Demographics"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col AGE     type=Num  label="Age"
col AGETXT  type=Char label="Age Range"
col ARMCD   type=Char label="Planned Arm Code"
---
S1 | DM | 001 | .  |       | Scrnfail
S1 | DM | 002 | .  |       | SCRNFAIL
